{"id":"G5007","lemma":"τάλαντον","transliteration":"talanton","sayIt":"talanton","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, neuter","gloss":"talent","meaning":"τάλαντομ, -ον, τ\n[in LXX for כִּכָּר ;]\n1. a balance (Hom.).\n2. that which is weighed, a talent;\n(a) a talent in weight (in Horn. always of gold);\n(b) a sum of money, whether gold or silver, equivalent to a talent in weight (see DB, iii, 418 ff.): Mat.18:24 25:15 ff.†\n(AS)","glosses":["talents","talent"],"count":8,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-18","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"talents"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"talents","kjv":"talents"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"talents","kjv":"talents"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"talents","kjv":"talents"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"talents","kjv":"alents"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"talent","kjv":"talent"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"talent","kjv":"talent"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"talent","kjv":"the talent"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 18:24","note":"When he had begun to reconcile, one was brought to him who owed him ten thousand talents.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}